/*! \page dirstructure ISCE3 Directory Structure

\tableofcontents

\section gitstructure Source folder structure 

The directory structure of the ISCE3 git repository is as shown below.
The repository might contain other hidden folders like ".cmake", ".mm", ".ci" etc
that contain configuration files for different build and CI systems.

\verbatim

.
├── CMakeLists.txt              (Main CMake file)
├── LICENSE
├── README.md
├── bin                         (Folder that holds executable scripts and entrypoints)
│   ├── crossmul.py
│   ├── geo2rdr.py
│   ├── isce3
│   ├── rdr2geo.py
│   └── resampSlc.py
├── cxx                         (C++ code)
│   ├── CMakeLists.txt
│   └── isce3                       - CPU only code
│       └── cuda                    - CUDA code
├── defaults                    (Pyre configurables)
│   └── isce3.pfg
├── doc                         (Documentation source)
│   ├── doxygen
│   └── sphinx
├── extern                      (External dependencies that are built with ISCE)
│   └── CMakeLists.txt
├── python                      (Python bindings for ISCE)
│   ├── CMakeLists.txt              
│   ├── extensions                  - C++ extensions using pybind11
│   └── packages                    - Pure python packages
└── tests                       (Unit tests)
    ├── CMakeLists.txt
    ├── cxx                         - C++ tests
    ├── data                        - Test data
    ├── extensions                  - Python extensions
    ├── extern                      - External dependencies built as part of ISCE
    └── python                      - Python bindings

\endverbatim


\section installstructure Installation folder structure

ISCE3 tries to follow the same directory structure as used by other open source projects like GDAL, FFTW etc.
Shown below are the contents of the sub-folders populated by ISCE3 below the installation folder.

\verbatim

.
├── include                     (C++ headers)
│   ├── Eigen
│   ├── isce3
├── lib                         (Shared libraries)
│   └── libisce3.0.dylib
├── packages                    (Python packages)
│   ├── isce3
│   └── nisar
└── share
    └── nisar                   (Examples/ tutorials folder)

\endverbatim



*/
